# One type, one file

Declare a struct (or named type) and **all** of its methods in a **single** source file. Do not scatter `(t *T)` / `(t T)` methods across files.

Package-level helpers (mapping, parsing, classification) may live in other files. Generated code (`ent/`, protos, mocks) is exempt.

```go
// BAD — Client methods split across client.go and shorts_prober.go
func (c *Client) GetLikedVideos(...)
func (c *Client) omitShorts(...) // shorts_prober.go

// GOOD — every Client method in client.go
// GOOD — mapDisplayableLikedVideo in displayable.go (not a method)
```

File for a method-bearing type is `snake_case(Type).go` (see also `pal-components`).

## Lint status

No golangci-lint linter enforces “all methods of a type in one file.”

- `funcorder` — order of constructors/methods **within** a file, not across files
- `recvcheck` — pointer vs value receiver consistency only

Rely on this rule + review. Do not invent a custom analyzer unless the team later chooses one.
